{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793612983,"nonce":"Q/7e66PIcQlEF21TiEeUWLg80vA=","message":"Landed in ac80e4f5 (engine) and 1efd1972 (cn). Owner chose the CSS engine design: motion_class on OverlayBuilder/ToastBuilder; wrapper carries data-motion enter/exit; reaped when css_animation_playing(id) shows its exit played (fallbacks 100ms never-started, 1000ms cap). Tabs use CssMotion via Row::on_leave, timed per frame. Engine fixes found on the way: (1) CSS animations inside an overlay root never showed when the subtree was plain divs: it was baked for a composite the overlay pass never runs; css_layer_bakeable now excludes overlay-root subtrees (popover/menu enter animations were affected too). (2) translate percentages in keyframes, resolved at animation start against the node size (ashui uses per-size custom props, which Blinc can't scope per element). (3) ActiveCssAnimation records its name so a rule naming another animation restarts it. (4) Headless harness now ticks overlay_stack/toast_tray update, rebuilds the toast layer, and settle waits for overlay transitions. Not done: the legacy OverlayManager (widgets/overlay.rs) still has Rust presets but no cn widget uses it; motion() itself has no CSS mode (overlays/toasts/tabs use CssMotion wrappers instead).","files":null}]}